<title>GERMANY: Details of German coalition tax plan.</title>
<headline>Details of German coalition tax plan.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of a German coalition government plan to reform the tax system through a two-stage reform in 1998 and 1999.</p>
<p>(Figures in billions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>						    Impact on tax revenues</p>
<p>						    Overall    1998    1999</p>
<p>1. Income taxes</p>
<p>15 pct rate on 13-18,000 DM</p>
<p>Sliding scale from 22.5 pct to</p>
<p>39 pct on 18-90,000</p>
<p>    Commercial income at 35 pct		-69.1	    -66.1</p>
<p>    Commercial income at 40 pct in '98		  -3.0</p>
<p>2. Other tax cuts</p>
<p>Corporation tax</p>
<p>35 pct on retained profits</p>
<p>    25 pct on distributed profits	    -9.8		-5.4</p>
<p>    Corporation tax 40/28 pct in '98		   -4.4</p>
<p>    Withholding tax 15 pct (vs 25 pct)     -0.5		-0.5</p>
<p>    Interest discount 25 pct (vs 35 pct)   -0.5		-0.5</p>
<p>    Lower revenues from solidarity tax     -2.0		-2.0</p>
<p> 3. GROSS TAX CUTS				-81.9    -7.4   -74.5</p>
<p> 4. Increased revs from wider tax base    +38.1    +7.4   +30.7</p>
<p> 5. NET TAX CUTS				  -43,8	     -43.8</p>
<p>6. Solidarity surcharge</p>
<p>    Cut to 5.5 pct (vs 7.5 pct) in '98		 -7.5</p>
<p>--Bonn newsroom +49 228 26097 150</p>
</text>
